  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Sitharaman urges ITRAF to make tax research more visible in policy process",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/finance/news/sitharaman-urges-itraf-to-make-tax-research-more-visible-in-policy-process-126091600591_1.html",
      "description": "Union Finance Minister Nirmala Sitharaman on Wednesday urged the International Tax Research and Analysis Foundation (ITRAF) to make its independent tax policy research more visible and contribute directly to policymaking and public discourse.\nAddressing the Eighth International Tax Conference on 'New Age Taxation' organised by ITRAF here, Sitharaman said India had professionals and experts of the highest calibre in taxation but needed stronger institutional platforms to bring their expertise together and contribute to policy choices.\n\"You have so far contributed quietly, and I would now urge you to contribute visibly, because I understand that the commentary you produce is of such high quality and it reaches the profession, but it should also reach the policy processes, and it should reach the public at large,\" she said.\nSitharaman said ITRAF had brought together chief financial officers and tax heads of major technology companies, senior advocates, partners of leading professional",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-09-16T09:21:08"
    },
    {
      "title": "Tax policy debate must go beyond sectoral interests: FM Sitharaman",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/industry/news/independent-tax-policy-research-should-enter-public-discourse-sitharaman-126091600445_1.html",
      "description": "Union Finance Minister Nirmala Sitharaman on Wednesday called for independent research on tax policy to become part of public discourse, saying tax professionals must look beyond sectoral interests and put the national interest first.\nSitharaman was speaking at the Eighth International Tax Conference on 'New Age Taxation' here organised by the International Tax Research and Analysis Foundation.\n\"A mature tax policy debate must go beyond sectoral considerations,\" she said, urging tax professionals to \"rise above sectoral consideration and put nation first.\"\nSitharaman said the government had deliberately rationalised provisions relating to Tax Deducted at Source (TDS) and Tax Collected at Source (TCS), raised thresholds and reduced unnecessary criminal consequences.\nOn international taxation, the finance minister said India renegotiated its tax treaties with Mauritius, Singapore and Cyprus to restore its right to tax capital gains at source.",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-09-16T07:22:54"
    },
    {
      "title": "35 yrs of liberalisation: Tax system makes progress, but reforms unfinished",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/economy/news/35-yrs-of-liberalisation-tax-system-makes-progress-but-reforms-unfinished-126091600016_1.html",
      "description": "India's tax system has come a long way since 1991, but simplifying GST, clearing tax disputes and improving taxpayer services remain key priorities",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-09-15T18:46:47"
    }
  ]
